{
  "gate": "arc-a770-bonsai25-27b-20261126",
  "title": "Arc A770: Bonsai 2.5 27B decodes on the device and matches the CPU engine",
  "measured": "2026-11-26",
  "commit": "unreleased",
  "command": "python -m kindi intel-step --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-2.5-27b --steps 4 --device-name \"Intel(R) Arc(TM) A770 Graphics\" --json docs/benchmarks/2026-11-26-i7-8086k-arc-a770-bonsai25-27b/step.json",
  "notes": "The 27B is the only size the 2.5 release has. Three fixes made it run: the driver's 4095 MiB per-allocation cap (codes chunked on tensor boundaries), the 27B's untied output.weight head (read from the manifest), and a 7.1 GB codes blob forced into RAM (now memory-mapped). intel-step is teacher-forced against cpu.Engine on the same pack; intel-run decodes a prompt with no CPU engine. Host math (conv, delta rule, attention, FFN elementwise) is still numpy; this is a probe, not a backend and not a speed claim.",
